{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794050396,"nonce":"NfthS/ewdoFvhB5TYrAEt0mfgL0=","title":"Steps before the approval gate write the Environment's cache scope","message":"A governed Run uses the cache scope `env:\u003cname\u003e` for every Step, including Steps before the Environment approval gate. A push to any branch whose Pipeline names `environment: prod`, with prod's allowed refs empty, writes `env:prod` before anyone approves, and a later approved deploy restores it.\n\nPull requests and fork Runs no longer get the Environment's scope (#100), but a branch push still does.\n\nProposed: Steps before a valid approval gate use their ref's scope, the same way they get the `env=none` OIDC subject.\n\nEvidence: red team RT-3 (K2), ~/.afk/scrarab-ci/20261107-0247-decisions/review/redteam.md, scratch test .workspaces/afk-redteam/crates/scarab-engine/tests/redteam_cache_scope.rs:48. Needs an owner decision.","files":null}]}